  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Welsh cawl is a lamb broth with leeks, potato, parsnip, and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "swede",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "swede"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The traditional method takes two days: the lamb simmers on the first day to make the stock, which sits overnight so the fat solidifies on top and can be lifted off. The vegetables then cook in the clear, skimmed stock the next day. You can do it in one day but the broth will be fattier. The two-day version is worth the patience."
          }
        ]
      },
